<article class="env-proposition" id="02M7">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02M7">Proposition <span data-tag="02M7">6.3.5.11</span>.</a> Let $f: X \rightarrow Y$ and $g: Y \rightarrow Z$ be universally localizing morphisms of simplicial sets. Then the composition $(g \circ f): X \rightarrow Z$ is universally localizing. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      Suppose we are given a morphism of simplicial sets $Z' \rightarrow Z$. Set $X' = Z' \times _{Z} X$, and let $W$ be the collection of those edges $w$ of $X'$ having degenerate image in $Z'$. We will show that the projection map $\pi : X' \rightarrow Z'$ exhibits $Z'$ as a localization of $X'$ with respect to $W$. Set $Y' = Z' \times _{Z} Y$, so that $\pi $ factors as a composition $X' \xrightarrow {f'} Y' \xrightarrow {g'} Z'$. It follows from Proposition <a data-tag="02M6" href="/tag/02M6">6.3.5.10</a> (and Remark <a data-tag="02M5" href="/tag/02M5">6.3.5.8</a>) that $f'$ is a surjection of simplicial sets. In particular, the image $f'(W)$ is the collection of all edges $u$ of $Y'$ having the property that $g'(u)$ is a degenerate edge of $Z'$. 
    <p>
      Let $W_0 \subseteq W$ be the collection of those edges $w$ of $X'$ for which $f'(w)$ is a degenerate edge of $Y'$. Applying Proposition <a data-tag="02M1" href="/tag/02M1">6.3.5.4</a>, we conclude that $f'$ exhibits $Y'$ as a localization of $X'$ with respect to $W_0$, and that $g'$ exhibits $Z'$ as a localization of $Y'$ with respect to $f'(W)$. Applying Proposition <a data-tag="02LS" href="/tag/02LS">6.3.1.22</a>, we conclude that $\pi = g' \circ f'$ exhibits $Z'$ as the localization of $X'$ with respect to $W_0 \cup W = W$, as desired. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
